The network is fully healthy. The DNS service on dns_server (10.200.0.2) is
operational: BIND 9.18 is running, its configuration passes named-checkconf
with no errors, and the authoritative "local" zone (serial 2025111101) is
loaded with correct A-records for web0.local through web3.local (10.200.0.3–
10.200.0.6). Both end-hosts resolve all four names correctly via getent and
dig, and curl confirms HTTP 200 responses when connecting by hostname from
host_1_1_1_1. The OSPF routing fabric is fully converged: all routers
(router_core_1/2/3, switch_dist_1_1/2_1, switch_server_access) have
complete FIB entries for every subnet, and ping confirms end-to-end IP
reachability from host_1_1_1_1 to the DNS server and all web servers. The
recursion no setting in named.conf is by design — the server is
authoritative-only for the internal zone and recursion is not needed. The
premise stated in ticket #8842 ("the name server must be dead") is incorrect.
There is no anomaly, no misconfiguration, and no device at fault. The
reported symptom is either a transient client-side glitch that has since
self-resolved, or was caused by a momentary issue external to this lab
(e.g., the Kathara lab had not yet fully converged when the user first
tested). No corrective action is required.
